no handedness and can be mounted either face up (holes are symmetric in both X and Y).\"],\"manufacturing_method\":\"3d_print_fdm\",\"special_features\":[\"Plate MUST be a single rectangular prism of PLATE_LENGTH_X x PLATE_WIDTH_Y x PLATE_THICKNESS_Z, centered on the origin in X and Y with Z=0 at the bottom face (origin_convention = centroid_on_base_plane).\",\"Fillet MUST be applied to ALL FOUR top perimeter edges bounding the top face at Z=PLATE_THICKNESS_Z (both the two long X-parallel edges and the two short Y-parallel edges) — MUST NOT fillet only two edges, and MUST NOT fillet any bottom edge.\",\"Fillet radius MUST be FILLET_RADIUS = 6.0 mm; because this exceeds PLATE_THICKNESS_Z (5 mm), if the CAD kernel rejects R6 the fallback MUST be a full-round of radius FILLET_MAX_FEASIBLE_RADIUS = 5.0 mm applied to the same four top edges, rather than leaving any top edge sharp.\",\"Fillets MUST be applied AFTER the plate is extruded and MUST be applied to the four top edges of the resulting prismatic solid (use edge selectors on the top face at Z=PLATE_THICKNESS_Z, e.g. edges grouped by Z == bounding box max).\",\"All four mounting holes MUST be through-holes with their axis parallel to the Z axis (Cylinder extruded / cut along Z through the full PLATE_THICKNESS_Z), MUST NOT be blind holes and MUST NOT be drilled along X or Y.\",\"The four holes MUST be placed one per corner at (X, Y) = (+/-HOLE_POS_X, +/-HOLE_POS_Y) = (+/-40, +/-15) mm, each exactly HOLE_EDGE_OFFSET = 10 mm from the two adjacent plate edges; they MUST NOT be placed on the plate centrelines or at the plate corners.\",\"The hole pattern MUST be symmetric about both the XZ plane (Y mirrors about Y=0) and the YZ plane (X mirrors about X=0).\",\"All four holes MUST have identical diameter HOLE_DIAMETER = 4.0 mm (radius HOLE_RADIUS = 2.0 mm) and MUST NOT be chamfered, countersunk, counterbored or threaded.\",\"Holes MUST be cut AFTER the top-edge fillets have been created so the fillets cannot intersect or